ents are divided horizontally, their X-coordinate ranges are unified by taking the union of their individual spans, explaining the wider output columns seen in Train 2. This same principle appears to apply to Train 1's horizontal divisions as well.\n\n**Analyzing Vertical Splits**\n\nI'm finding that for vertical splits, the Y-coordinate ranges are indeed shared and unified, appearing to be the full height. However, it seems the X-coordinate ranges for each part are then cropped independently to their respective foreground element spans.\n\n",
